=== Kit information ===
This is Adidas's 13th year supplying Flamengo kit during its second stint with the team, having taken over from [[Olympikus]] at the beginning of the 2013 season.<ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.sambafoot.com/en/news/40523_flamengo_approve____150_million_adidas_kit_deal.html |title=Flamengo approve €150 million Adidas kit deal |date=20 December 2012 |publisher=sambafoot.com |access-date=27 February 2020}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=http://www.sportspromedia.com/news/flamengo_announce_record_adidas_deal |title=Flamengo announce record Adidas deal |date=21 December 2012 |publisher=sportspromedia.com |access-date=27 February 2020}}</ref> The deal was renewed for another 5 seasons on 29 April 2024.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://ge.globo.com/futebol/times/flamengo/noticia/2024/04/29/flamengo-renova-com-fornecedora-de-material-esportivo-veja-detalhes-do-novo-contrato.ghtml |title=Flamengo renova com fornecedora de material esportivo; veja detalhes do novo contrato |publisher=ge.globo |language=pt-BR |date=29 April 2024 |access-date=9 June 2025}}</ref>

*'''Home:''' The club revealed their new home kit for the 2026 season on 16 January. The kit maintain Flamengo's traditional colours of red and black and references the club's kits used in the 1980s, also produced by Adidas during its first stint. The shirt has a polo collar without buttons and its body is predominantly black (just like the previous two seasons) and contains three large black stripes and two large red stripes. It's complemented by white shorts and red socks with a large black stripe.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ge.globo.com/futebol/times/flamengo/noticia/2026/01/16/flamengo-lanca-uniforme-principal-para-a-temporada-2026-veja-fotos.ghtml|title=Flamengo lança uniforme principal para a temporada 2026; veja fotos|publisher=ge.globo.com|date=2026-01-16|access-date=2026-01-16}}</ref>
*'''"Away":''' On 10 April, Flamengo released their second kit and retires the term "Away", referring to the kit as "''Manto 1 Branco''" ("White Home kit" in context). The shirt has a white body with two horizontal stripes (red on the top stripe and black on the bottom stripe) centered at chest level, which were last used in 2019. It's complemented by black shorts and white socks<ref>{{cite web|url=https://ge.globo.com/futebol/times/flamengo/noticia/2026/04/10/flamengo-lanca-novo-uniforme-para-a-temporada-2026-veja-fotos.ghtml|title=Flamengo lança novo uniforme para a temporada 2026; veja fotos|publisher=ge.globo.com|date=2026-04-10|access-date=2026-04-25}}</ref>
*'''GK:''' The new goalkeeper kits are based on Adidas' goalkeeper template for the 2026–27 season.

